Falsifies `system_tests::user::futex_tests::a_waiter_sleeps_until_its_word_is_woken`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: `AddressSpace::WAIT` returns "woken" instead of parking when the word still holds what
the waiter expected, so a futex never sleeps and every lock built on it becomes a spin.

Expected to fail: "the waiter never parked on its word", with the waiter having returned hundreds
of thousands of times (replayed on all three architectures, 2026-10-10 UTC).

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched.rs b/kernel/src/sched.rs
--- a/kernel/src/sched.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched.rs
@@ -3480,6 +3480,9 @@ pub fn futex_wait(space: u64, va: u64, expected: u32) -> Result<u64, abi::Error>
         if word != expected {
             return Ok(1);
         }
+        if word == expected {
+            return Ok(0);
+        }
         let current = current_thread_id();
         let token = take_token(sched, current);
         sched.futexes.park(key, token);
